{"variant":"base","mode":"judged","bead":"hv-umm2.51","commit":"5f8304aa1907903e1825ade9ec5dfbaf72ae258d","uuid":"5ab11bef-5dcd-49f5-be49-ae2ccde76e70","as":"player","verdict":"pass","screens":["colossus-desktop-ready.png","colossus-desktop-hover.png","support-desktop-board.png","colossus-mobile-ready.png","support-mobile-board.png","support-mobile-log.png"],"notes":"D21 SHA-256 sample (first byte 0x01). Desktop 1440x900 and mobile 390x844, as=player. Check 1: green playable outline at 10/10 energy. Checks 2-3: no prompt or targets (none printed). Check 4: plays to the stack, enters B0 exhausted at 6 spark (zero supporters in the back rank, C9); a debug-added Colossus moved to F0 reads 8 with one back-rank supporter (the exhausted Colossus in B0, no Support keyword) and 12 once Nocturne Strummer moves into B1 (6 + 2x2 supporters + Strummer's +2); the spark badge updates live after each reposition and the hover card shows 12; log reads 'You played Rusted Colossus.', 'Rusted Colossus entered play.' and each move. Check 5: no duration. Check 7: no clipping; __caps empty throughout."}
{"variant":"base","mode":"judged","bead":"hv-umm2.51","commit":"5f8304aa1907903e1825ade9ec5dfbaf72ae258d","uuid":"5ab11bef-5dcd-49f5-be49-ae2ccde76e70","as":"enemy","verdict":"pass","screens":["colossus-enemy-desktop-stack.png","colossus-enemy-desktop-log.png","colossus-enemy-mobile-stack.png","colossus-enemy-mobile-log.png"],"notes":"Desktop and mobile, as=enemy. Respond-or-Pass banner names Rusted Colossus with the card revealed at reading size and Pass enabled; after Pass it enters the enemy back rank at 6 spark and the log reads 'Rusted Colossus entered play.'; __caps empty; layout fits at both sizes."}
{"variant":"base","mode":"judged","bead":"hv-umm2.51","commit":"5f8304aa1907903e1825ade9ec5dfbaf72ae258d","uuid":"5a980eff-6ec7-44d8-9977-b98e66bbc2c8","as":"player","verdict":"pass","screens":["support-desktop-board.png","support-mobile-board.png","support-mobile-log.png"],"notes":"Judged for its Support aura (status indicator). Desktop and mobile, as=player, on the Rusted Colossus board: Strummer in B1 gives F0 (Rusted Colossus) and F1 (Final Witness 2 -> 4) +2 spark each; moving it from B2 into B1 changes F0's badge from 8 to 12 at once, and B0's back-rank Colossus stays 6 (back-rank characters are not supported); hover shows the Support glossary entry; repositions are logged; __caps empty; no clipping."}
{"variant":"base","mode":"judged","bead":"hv-umm2.51","commit":"5f8304aa1907903e1825ade9ec5dfbaf72ae258d","uuid":"5a980eff-6ec7-44d8-9977-b98e66bbc2c8","as":"enemy","verdict":"pass","screens":["strummer-enemy-desktop-stack.png","strummer-enemy-desktop-log.png","strummer-enemy-mobile-stack.png","strummer-enemy-mobile-log.png"],"notes":"Desktop and mobile, as=enemy: banner names Nocturne Strummer with its card revealed; after Pass it enters the enemy back rank at 1 spark and the log reads 'Nocturne Strummer entered play.'; __caps empty; layout fits."}
{"variant":"base","mode":"judged","bead":"hv-umm2.51","commit":"5f8304aa1907903e1825ade9ec5dfbaf72ae258d","uuid":"944e15d2-d680-4ebe-8d18-36826f4b1535","as":"player","verdict":"pass","screens":["worlds-await-desktop-ready.png","worlds-await-desktop-two-targets.png","worlds-await-desktop-target.png","worlds-await-desktop-log.png","worlds-await-mobile-targets.png","worlds-await-mobile-resolved.png"],"notes":"Judged for its spark gain (status indicator). Desktop and mobile, as=player. Check 1: green playable outline. Checks 2-3: with one own character the target is answered automatically; with a second own character added, 'Choose a target / From Worlds Await' highlights exactly the two own characters (enemy has none), Cancel returns the card to hand with energy refunded, and choosing Final Witness resolves. Check 4: the target's badge goes 2 -> 5 (0 -> 3 on the lab character), Worlds Await goes to the void, log reads 'You played Worlds Await.' then '<target>: +3 spark.'. Check 5: permanent gain, no duration indicator expected. Check 7: no clipping (the dev-only debug button grazes the Cancel button's right edge at 390 wide but Cancel's centre hits; see pre-existing); __caps empty."}
{"variant":"base","mode":"judged","bead":"hv-umm2.51","commit":"5f8304aa1907903e1825ade9ec5dfbaf72ae258d","uuid":"944e15d2-d680-4ebe-8d18-36826f4b1535","as":"enemy","verdict":"fail","screens":["worlds-await-enemy-desktop-stack.png","worlds-await-enemy-desktop-resolving.png","worlds-await-enemy-desktop-log.png","worlds-await-enemy-mobile-stack.png","worlds-await-enemy-mobile-resolved.png"],"notes":"Desktop and mobile, as=enemy. Pass: banner 'Respond or Pass / Worlds Await is waiting to resolve' with the card revealed and Pass enabled; after Pass the enemy character's badge goes 0 -> 3, the card goes to the enemy void, log reads 'Card: +3 spark.'; __caps empty; layout fits. Fail (check 6, targets shown): while the enemy's Worlds Await waits on the stack, nothing on the board marks the character it targets (the stack item's chosen target i10 is in the view's stack targets, but EngineBattleScreen renders no stack-target marker), so the human cannot see what the response window is about. Root cause outside the bead's areas: the battle screen (src/battle/components/EngineBattleScreen.tsx and the board card presentation) needs a marker on each visible target of a stack item; it affects every targeted enemy card."}
{"variant":"base","mode":"judged","bead":"hv-umm2.51","commit":"5f8304aa1907903e1825ade9ec5dfbaf72ae258d","uuid":"647f5150-b2e0-424b-9480-27557642524e","as":"player","verdict":"fail","screens":["ringwatcher-desktop-foresee.png","ringwatcher-mobile-foresee.png","ringwatcher-mobile-foresee-void.png","ringwatcher-mobile-log.png"],"notes":"Judged as the first catalog card with the Foresee prompt. Desktop and mobile, as=player. Pass: playable outline; the ▸Materialized trigger opens the Foresee 1 editor with the top card between Deck and Void, not cancellable (a trigger), Confirm resolves; dragging the card to Void and confirming puts it in the void; __caps empty; layout fits. Fail (check 4, battle log): the log reads only 'You played Ringwatcher.', 'Ringwatcher entered play.', 'Ringwatcher's triggered ability resolved.'; nothing says a Foresee happened or that a card went to the void, because the foresee primitive moves cards with no engine event. Fix outside the areas: a foresee event kind (cards kept and voided, the voided ones public) emitted by src/engine/effects/primitives/foresee.ts, with its EVENT_PRESENTATION entry (src/battle/components/presentation-items.ts), prompt-lab fixture (src/engine/testing/prompt-lab.ts) and log line (src/runtime/battle-prompt-messages.ts)."}
{"variant":"base","mode":"judged","bead":"hv-umm2.51","commit":"5f8304aa1907903e1825ade9ec5dfbaf72ae258d","uuid":"647f5150-b2e0-424b-9480-27557642524e","as":"enemy","verdict":"fail","screens":["ringwatcher-enemy-desktop-choosing.png","ringwatcher-enemy-desktop-log.png","ringwatcher-enemy-mobile-choosing.png","ringwatcher-enemy-mobile-log.png"],"notes":"Desktop and mobile, as=enemy. Pass: banner names Ringwatcher; after Pass it enters the enemy back rank, the AI answers its private Foresee without exposing the card; __caps empty; layout fits. Fail (check 6): the log reads only 'Ringwatcher entered play.' and 'Ringwatcher's triggered ability resolved.', so the human cannot tell that the opponent foresaw or whether a card went to its void. Same root cause and fix as the as=player line."}
